WEBVTT

00:04.010 --> 00:06.480
<i>With all these votes secured,</i>

00:06.480 --> 00:09.360
<i>I'm guaranteed to become hospital director.</i>

00:09.360 --> 00:11.490
Hello there, Professor Goldran.

00:11.490 --> 00:13.240
Lord Fennel.

00:13.240 --> 00:18.370
As my savior, it's appropriate that you'll 
finally have standing to reflect that.

00:18.620 --> 00:22.250
Thank you for such generous praise.

00:22.570 --> 00:24.960
<i>I've finally made it here...</i>

00:25.900 --> 00:30.390
<i>It all began with that explosion in the 
magic tool factory thirteen years ago.</i>

00:30.960 --> 00:35.470
<i>That day, I was heading back to my hometown 
after my research yielded no results.</i>

00:35.470 --> 00:39.600
<i>I thought that if I saved an aristocrat's life, 
their gratitude could get me somewhere.</i>

00:40.080 --> 00:41.600
<i>It was the first time</i>

00:41.600 --> 00:45.870
<i>I had successfully used my health transfer 
magic with a donor other than myself.</i>

00:46.310 --> 00:51.200
<i>Lord Fennel being one of the seven great 
nobles was an unexpected windfall.</i>

00:51.690 --> 00:55.070
<i>The only downside was that Bons 
captured the moment on camera,</i>

00:55.070 --> 00:57.820
<i>which led me to give him the 
position of first secretary,</i>

00:57.820 --> 01:00.380
<i>and the lifestyle that came 
with it, to keep him quiet.</i>

01:01.580 --> 01:03.370
I'll see you later, then.

01:04.720 --> 01:06.870
Well, this is impressive!

01:07.590 --> 01:10.750
You've really made something 
of yourself, Professor Goldran.

01:11.130 --> 01:12.860
Ah, Becker.

01:13.990 --> 01:17.380
Here to ingratiate yourself with 
the next director already?

01:17.640 --> 01:21.140
I don't have a problem with 
you seeing it that way.

01:21.140 --> 01:26.450
That special research student was 
here on your recommendation, yes?

01:26.450 --> 01:28.620
I had taken a shine to him, 
thinking he'd be useful,

01:28.620 --> 01:30.650
but he turned out to be a waste of time.

01:30.650 --> 01:32.570
Did he offend you somehow?

01:32.570 --> 01:35.280
He was invited to one of my dinner parties,

01:35.280 --> 01:38.090
yet chose to leave to heal some 
demihumans who barged in.

01:38.090 --> 01:40.060
An act of inconceivable idiocy.

01:41.780 --> 01:46.790
A member of my faction cannot 
prioritize peasants for healing.

01:46.790 --> 01:49.300
He needs to consider our position as healers.

01:49.750 --> 01:52.500
Not all lives have equal value.

02:08.070 --> 02:15.580
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

03:25.400 --> 03:29.980
Looking back now, my relationship with 
Professor Goldran began thirteen years ago,

03:29.980 --> 03:32.270
when, after I had been seriously wounded—

03:32.270 --> 03:33.640
Lord Fennel.

03:33.640 --> 03:35.840
I'm sure there's no need 
to share such a sad story.

03:35.840 --> 03:39.470
Oh? It seems our star would rather 
not discuss his past glories.

03:39.470 --> 03:44.620
How humble is that, for someone on the 
verge of becoming the next director?

03:46.050 --> 03:49.330
Well, let's hear from the man himself, then.

03:49.330 --> 03:51.330
It's an honor, sir.

03:52.080 --> 03:56.290
<i>At this moment, my life has reached its apex.</i>

03:57.710 --> 04:01.090
I propose a toast to our bright future!

04:03.590 --> 04:05.780
Is this from thirteen years ago?

04:06.220 --> 04:10.250
Dr. Becker mentioned meeting 
Mr. Bons yesterday,

04:10.250 --> 04:12.070
but I wasn't expecting this.

04:12.980 --> 04:16.690
He looks pretty young in the picture, 
but I'm pretty sure this is Afread!

04:16.690 --> 04:20.230
Then the theory of him surviving 
this accident is true.

04:22.440 --> 04:23.610
Why?!

04:24.070 --> 04:26.230
This woman is...

04:29.640 --> 04:31.010
What's happened?

04:35.250 --> 04:36.900
Becker?

04:36.900 --> 04:38.210
It's poison, Professor.

04:38.210 --> 04:39.420
Poison?!

04:39.840 --> 04:42.460
Mixed in with the wine 
that we all toasted with.

04:43.120 --> 04:45.530
Poison and medicine are two 
sides of the same coin.

04:45.530 --> 04:48.720
And preparing medicine is my specialty.

04:49.490 --> 04:51.180
What is this?!

04:52.000 --> 04:56.160
It's a toxin that causes loss of consciousness 
before gradually ending one's life.

04:56.160 --> 04:59.820
Which should occur in roughly 
one hour, without intervention.

04:59.820 --> 05:04.330
The dose in your glass was slightly weaker,

05:04.330 --> 05:07.070
but still, I'd wager you won't last two hours.

05:07.070 --> 05:09.200
What do you think you're doing?!

05:09.200 --> 05:10.590
Isn't it obvious?

05:11.150 --> 05:13.320
Recreating that moment 
from thirteen years ago.

05:13.320 --> 05:16.780
You... How do you know about that?!

05:17.210 --> 05:20.720
I've had my suspicions for a while now,

05:20.720 --> 05:25.220
but it was our talented special research 
student who made it clear to me.

05:25.220 --> 05:28.090
What did he do now?

05:28.090 --> 05:30.660
He found a lead for me to follow.

05:30.660 --> 05:33.040
And Mr. Bons was reluctant to talk,

05:33.040 --> 05:36.230
so I used a combination of alcohol 
and medicine to loosen his lips.

05:36.230 --> 05:38.950
Finding the picture was pure luck, though.

05:38.950 --> 05:40.700
I thought I had gotten rid of that...

05:40.700 --> 05:43.390
He had another copy, apparently.

05:43.390 --> 05:45.830
Looks like you're a poor judge of character.

05:45.830 --> 05:47.200
Shut up!

05:47.200 --> 05:49.650
"Not all lives have equal value."

05:50.260 --> 05:53.380
Professor Goldran, thirteen years ago,

05:53.380 --> 05:56.570
that belief led you to 
choose whose life to save...

05:57.210 --> 06:00.560
and to sacrifice the lives of others.

06:00.560 --> 06:02.960
They would have died anyway!

06:02.960 --> 06:04.760
In your estimation, at least.

06:04.760 --> 06:08.000
But Afread was among their number.

06:09.520 --> 06:12.220
As was my fiancée.

06:13.720 --> 06:17.810
I've ensured you have enough strength 
left to use health transfer magic.

06:17.810 --> 06:22.310
Preventing the poison's progression 
will require a fair bit of life force,

06:22.690 --> 06:25.050
but there are plenty of lives here to use.

06:25.690 --> 06:28.180
So, who will you sacrifice this time?

06:28.180 --> 06:30.070
Who will you save?

06:30.070 --> 06:31.950
Your own life?

06:31.950 --> 06:37.080
Lord Fennel? Or the members of the 
faction who've given their votes to you?

06:37.080 --> 06:40.430
Go on. It's time to choose who lives.

06:42.250 --> 06:46.530
I know! An antidote! 
There must be one, right?!

06:46.530 --> 06:47.870
Give it to me now!

06:47.870 --> 06:50.470
And I'll see that your 
punishment isn't too harsh.

06:52.990 --> 06:54.550
What are you doing?

06:55.960 --> 06:58.960
I took a small enough dose 
to retain consciousness...

06:58.960 --> 07:01.190
But it really does have 
quite a kick, doesn't it?

07:01.190 --> 07:04.290
And now I'm poisoned myself.

07:05.320 --> 07:08.520
You have one more option now.

07:08.520 --> 07:12.950
You can believe that I have an antidote 
and save my life, if you like.

07:12.950 --> 07:16.010
You can't think you'll get away with this.

07:16.010 --> 07:21.580
I'd stay focused if I were you, 
or you'll run out of lives to exploit.

07:21.580 --> 07:24.590
Damn you!

07:25.170 --> 07:26.660
<i>Who do I save?</i>

07:26.660 --> 07:28.160
<i>Myself first.</i>

07:28.160 --> 07:30.340
<i>Then Lord Fennel.</i>

07:30.340 --> 07:33.840
<i>If there's no guarantee 
that he has an antidote,</i>

07:33.840 --> 07:35.970
<i>then the sacrifice should be...</i>

07:36.290 --> 07:39.440
Woven into a single ray of light,

07:39.440 --> 07:42.640
let the lost embers of life be your guide,

07:42.640 --> 07:45.100
so that they may find their way home.

07:45.100 --> 07:46.700
Give Heal!

07:47.560 --> 07:50.570
That is your choice, then?

07:50.880 --> 07:54.820
They have a duty to serve me.

07:55.150 --> 07:56.720
That's a shame.

07:56.720 --> 08:01.840
I already told you, your dose 
was weaker than the others'.

08:01.840 --> 08:03.900
What difference does that make?

08:03.900 --> 08:08.670
That means you have the most 
life force among everyone here.

08:09.090 --> 08:13.770
If you had used that life force, you could 
have saved the largest number of people.

08:13.770 --> 08:17.100
I am worth more than other healers!

08:17.100 --> 08:21.350
Then you insist that not 
all life is of equal value?

08:21.350 --> 08:22.710
Obviously!

08:22.710 --> 08:27.060
Even among coins, you have 
gold, silver, and bronze!

08:27.060 --> 08:28.940
Life is the same way!

08:28.940 --> 08:32.060
What sense does it make to 
not save the most worthy?!

08:36.180 --> 08:37.380
Well, now...

08:38.830 --> 08:40.580
Dr. Becker!

08:40.580 --> 08:42.990
Umin? What are you doing here?

08:44.400 --> 08:46.820
We found a picture in your room,

08:46.820 --> 08:50.090
and your former fiancée was in it.

08:50.470 --> 08:52.460
I got a bad feeling.

08:52.770 --> 08:54.340
You poisoned them?

08:54.340 --> 08:55.750
Zenos...

08:56.480 --> 08:59.970
Dr. Becker, why would you do this?!

09:01.040 --> 09:03.620
Are all lives equally valuable?

09:03.620 --> 09:06.440
I've considered the question for a long time.

09:06.790 --> 09:11.490
Thirteen years ago, my fiancée 
and I were rookie healers.

09:12.550 --> 09:16.820
Her eyes would shine as she talked about 
all the lives she wanted to save.

09:17.450 --> 09:22.580
When I heard she was caught 
in an explosion and died,

09:22.580 --> 09:24.830
the ruthlessness of death,

09:24.830 --> 09:26.960
and God's lack of mercy,

09:26.960 --> 09:28.730
drove me into the depths of grief.

09:30.990 --> 09:32.990
If it had just been a random accident,

09:32.990 --> 09:37.370
I would've carried on in her place, 
trying to save other people.

09:37.840 --> 09:43.150
But after attending that dinner party, 
Afread told me that it wasn't an accident,

09:43.150 --> 09:46.100
and that Goldran was involved.

09:46.100 --> 09:48.040
That's what happened?

09:48.560 --> 09:51.800
It was the last thing he 
said to me before vanishing.

09:52.400 --> 09:56.930
And the thought of my fiancée having been 
murdered rather than dying in an accident...

09:56.930 --> 09:59.010
I couldn't maintain my composure.

09:59.700 --> 10:03.830
But without any evidence, 
and with Afread missing,

10:03.830 --> 10:06.250
I couldn't pursue the truth, either.

10:07.210 --> 10:09.460
Which is why you hired me.

10:09.460 --> 10:11.780
Ideally, you'd find Afread.

10:11.780 --> 10:16.090
But, if nothing else, you could get into the 
dinner party and get some kind of information.

10:16.090 --> 10:18.090
But... This is just...

10:18.090 --> 10:20.140
Umin, I'm so sorry.

10:21.170 --> 10:22.320
But I—

10:22.320 --> 10:24.350
Shut up!

10:24.640 --> 10:25.750
Cresson?

10:26.270 --> 10:27.420
Look, I get it.

10:27.420 --> 10:31.010
If something that messed up 
had happened to my lover,

10:31.010 --> 10:32.440
I wouldn't be able to take it.

10:32.440 --> 10:34.190
Even though I don't have one!

10:34.510 --> 10:39.070
And you're right about one thing: Goldran over 
there is a huge piece of crap. No doubt about it.

10:39.070 --> 10:40.280
You wretch!

10:40.280 --> 10:43.190
But this isn't it!

10:43.190 --> 10:45.090
It's not right!

10:45.090 --> 10:48.410
Wanting revenge so badly, you poison 
people who have nothing to do with it?!

10:48.410 --> 10:50.420
That's not how it should be!

10:51.380 --> 10:53.230
Aren't you a healer?!

10:53.230 --> 10:57.430
I thought we were supposed to save people!

10:57.430 --> 10:59.130
Well said, Cresson.

11:00.110 --> 11:03.930
Hey, Becker, remember when you asked me

11:03.930 --> 11:08.430
which coins I would pick up when a 
bunch were scattered on the ground?

11:08.790 --> 11:10.300
It was a stupid question.

11:10.860 --> 11:12.420
I'd pick them all up.

11:12.900 --> 11:14.430
All of them?

11:14.430 --> 11:17.150
I grew up poor, you know.

11:18.030 --> 11:21.280
You seriously intend to save everyone?

11:21.280 --> 11:24.780
Why? How does it benefit you?

11:24.780 --> 11:29.160
It's true that I've already 
finished the job you hired me for,

11:29.160 --> 11:33.600
but if I don't do anything, you're 
gonna end up guilty of mass murder.

11:33.600 --> 11:35.670
And there's someone who'd 
be worse off if that happened.

11:35.930 --> 11:37.580
Zenos...

11:37.580 --> 11:40.300
Will you save them?

11:40.300 --> 11:42.140
It's payback for the going-away party.

11:42.730 --> 11:46.740
Never had someone say they were 
sad to see me leave before.

11:46.740 --> 11:49.420
Normally, people get sick 
of me, and I get kicked out.

11:49.930 --> 11:54.040
Zenos, you intend to save these people,

11:54.040 --> 11:59.650
but it's difficult to provide accurate antidote 
magic without knowing the specifics of the toxin.

11:59.930 --> 12:02.530
You gonna tell me the details, then?

12:02.530 --> 12:05.440
Do you even know them yourself?

12:05.440 --> 12:06.530
What are you—

12:06.530 --> 12:09.450
Never mind. Don't have a lot of time, anyway.

12:12.450 --> 12:12.910
Heal!

12:15.630 --> 12:18.670
Heal? A normal Heal spell?!

12:19.340 --> 12:21.350
That might repair the damage it does,

12:21.350 --> 12:24.050
but it won't purge the poison 
from their systems!

12:24.050 --> 12:27.680
I can encourage the body's 
natural healing, though.

12:27.680 --> 12:29.640
Those effects are temporary!

12:29.640 --> 12:31.330
The poison has already spread to—

12:32.990 --> 12:34.140
Don't tell me...

12:34.440 --> 12:36.400
I'm no toxicologist,

12:36.400 --> 12:38.770
but the effects must wear off sooner or later.

12:39.080 --> 12:44.320
You seriously intend to heal all these 
people until the poison has run its course?!

12:44.780 --> 12:47.650
It's an endurance test between 
the poison and my healing magic.

12:48.480 --> 12:51.110
You'd be surprised 
how competitive I can be.

12:58.340 --> 13:00.590
You are just...

13:00.590 --> 13:02.370
I got your back, Bro!

13:02.370 --> 13:03.840
Likewise!

13:03.840 --> 13:06.490
Focus your healing on 
whoever looks the weakest!

13:06.490 --> 13:07.470
Right!

13:06.490 --> 13:07.470
Got it!

13:11.140 --> 13:14.640
You have a subordinate and an 
underclassman cleaning up your mess.

13:14.640 --> 13:16.350
You'd better be grateful.

13:16.350 --> 13:20.960
I can't believe you're capable of casting 
Heal over this length of time.

13:20.960 --> 13:23.680
That's not how this spell works.

13:23.680 --> 13:24.900
It's not?

13:25.360 --> 13:29.870
I already thought you were remarkable, 
but this is just absurd.

13:29.870 --> 13:32.530
I didn't get a proper education, after all.

13:33.710 --> 13:38.240
My fiancée became a healer to save lives.

13:38.240 --> 13:41.760
She was an admirable woman 
who had high-minded goals.

13:41.760 --> 13:42.530
Yeah.

13:43.590 --> 13:48.340
Goldran killed her... And the thought 
of him becoming the next director...

13:48.340 --> 13:50.540
I couldn't let that happen!

13:50.540 --> 13:54.960
I couldn't allow someone who was her 
opposite in every way to rise to the top!

13:54.960 --> 13:55.750
I know.

13:57.230 --> 14:01.080
The longer I've spent here, 
the more I've realized...

14:01.580 --> 14:03.400
There's so much disparity in the world.

14:03.990 --> 14:06.550
There are people who can afford 
the most advanced healing,

14:06.550 --> 14:09.480
and people who can barely afford 
the most meager medication.

14:09.480 --> 14:10.260
Yeah.

14:11.120 --> 14:14.780
"Are all lives equal in value?"

14:14.780 --> 14:18.990
That question may have consumed 
me more than I realized.

14:20.160 --> 14:23.120
Seeing them so desperate to save lives...

14:23.120 --> 14:27.440
Maybe they're the ones who have 
inherited my fiancée's spirit.

14:28.380 --> 14:30.760
Zenos, thank you.

14:31.340 --> 14:32.810
No thanks necessary.

14:33.350 --> 14:36.900
But I am tired as hell, 
so I'm gonna need bonus pay.

14:38.210 --> 14:40.140
W-Wait a moment!

14:40.730 --> 14:44.310
I haven't been healed!

14:44.310 --> 14:46.110
Oh. I forgot.

14:46.110 --> 14:48.000
Don't you mock me!

14:48.000 --> 14:51.700
I command you... to save me!

14:51.700 --> 14:53.920
I was kicked out of your faction,

14:53.920 --> 14:55.990
so I don't take orders from you.

14:55.990 --> 15:00.370
You people! Save me, damn it!

15:00.370 --> 15:03.670
It's only in fragments, but 
I remember what happened...

15:03.670 --> 15:07.780
After I lost consciousness, it felt 
like my life was being drained.

15:07.780 --> 15:12.620
Professor, were you going to sacrifice us?

15:13.850 --> 15:16.350
And that's what they think of your demands.

15:16.700 --> 15:20.600
But as long as I get my money, 
I don't play favorites.

15:20.910 --> 15:22.980
I'm an underground healer, after all.

15:22.980 --> 15:26.010
So if you want my help, it's gonna cost you.

15:26.010 --> 15:27.930
Cost me?

15:27.930 --> 15:32.360
Considering how tired I am, 
another round of healing is gonna take...

15:32.360 --> 15:33.970
about this much.

15:34.620 --> 15:38.000
Ridiculous! I'm not paying that amount!

15:38.000 --> 15:40.810
Yeah? Never mind, then.

15:40.810 --> 15:42.500
Wait, wait wait wait!

15:42.500 --> 15:45.340
I'll pay! You'll get your money. Just save me!

15:45.600 --> 15:47.210
Goldran.

15:47.210 --> 15:51.220
We're going to discuss this 
matter in detail later.

15:52.720 --> 15:56.350
Damn it... Damn it!

16:02.350 --> 16:04.880
I've never been interrogated before.

16:04.880 --> 16:06.860
Quite the experience!

16:07.220 --> 16:08.860
Dr. Becker...

16:08.860 --> 16:13.490
I have to say, considering the incident was 
yesterday and the investigation is ongoing,

16:13.490 --> 16:16.240
I'm impressed you got permission to see me.

16:16.240 --> 16:19.280
I actually have an acquaintance 
in the royal guard.

16:19.280 --> 16:20.460
You do?

16:21.800 --> 16:23.800
Good to see you again, Mr. Zenos.

16:24.250 --> 16:29.340
I'm touched that you'd use a meeting with 
a suspect as an excuse to come and see me.

16:29.340 --> 16:32.090
I'm, uh, not here to see you, actually.

16:33.760 --> 16:36.970
But I do appreciate you arranging this.

16:36.970 --> 16:38.220
Thank you.

16:38.220 --> 16:42.910
Please! It's nothing, 
considering what I owe you.

16:42.910 --> 16:46.350
Um... how do you two know each other?

16:46.350 --> 16:47.380
Don't worry about it.

16:48.610 --> 16:51.600
I came to ask you some questions today.

16:51.600 --> 16:53.740
Questions?

16:53.740 --> 16:58.240
Dr. Becker, you didn't actually 
poison anyone, did you?

16:58.240 --> 17:00.800
In a sense, yes. You're correct.

17:00.800 --> 17:02.070
In a sense?

17:02.500 --> 17:07.250
I would use a poison to create a situation 
like the one from thirteen years ago,

17:07.250 --> 17:13.340
and, under the pressure, 
Goldran would confess his crimes.

17:13.340 --> 17:16.250
That was my original plan.

17:16.250 --> 17:19.220
B-But you said you didn't poison anyone...

17:19.220 --> 17:23.980
I had prepared a drug that would 
only temporarily paralyze the body.

17:24.560 --> 17:29.260
My intention was to lie to Goldran 
about it being a lethal toxin.

17:30.070 --> 17:34.090
At first, I thought I had made a 
mistake in preparing the drug,

17:34.090 --> 17:35.660
but that wasn't it.

17:35.660 --> 17:38.710
The natural conclusion is 
that someone other than me

17:38.710 --> 17:42.370
tampered with the wine, 
using a different chemical.

17:42.370 --> 17:44.500
And you think that was Afread?

17:44.500 --> 17:46.160
Most likely.

17:46.740 --> 17:49.580
He may have been there that night.

17:49.580 --> 17:51.590
Pretending to take a dose of the poison,

17:51.590 --> 17:55.840
blending in among the collapsed healers, 
and watching how events unfolded.

17:55.840 --> 17:58.180
Then Afread would be the one who—

17:58.180 --> 18:01.070
No. I'm still guilty.

18:01.470 --> 18:04.630
I realized there was an 
actual poison in the wine,

18:04.630 --> 18:06.600
but I was desperate.

18:06.600 --> 18:10.640
At that point, I didn't care if 
everyone died, including myself.

18:11.200 --> 18:12.760
Dr. Becker...

18:13.360 --> 18:16.010
You don't need to worry about him.

18:16.010 --> 18:20.270
Considering he didn't intend to poison
anyone and he's an acquaintance of yours,

18:20.270 --> 18:24.530
I can use my authority as vice captain 
of the order to see him released.

18:24.530 --> 18:27.250
Maybe go through due process instead?

18:27.250 --> 18:32.330
If it's a request of yours, Mr. Zenos, 
I'm prepared to bare it all,

18:32.330 --> 18:33.960
embarrassing though it might be.

18:33.960 --> 18:35.500
What are you even talking about?

18:36.660 --> 18:39.970
I don't care what authority you 
have to use! Please, do it!

18:43.360 --> 18:44.350
Zenos.

18:45.240 --> 18:46.040
What's up?

18:46.680 --> 18:49.100
I'm sure you've realized, but...

18:49.100 --> 18:51.900
You're talking about the 
Afread in the picture, right?

18:51.900 --> 18:54.660
It's hard to believe he survived 
having his life drained by Goldran,

18:54.660 --> 18:56.610
considering the situation.

18:56.610 --> 19:01.490
Right. Which raises the question: 
who was the Afread I encountered?

19:01.800 --> 19:04.400
Or maybe... <i>What</i> was he?

19:04.400 --> 19:08.360
This may not be as simple as 
revenge for thirteen years ago.

19:08.870 --> 19:12.830
And you were the one who foiled his plans.

19:13.150 --> 19:17.710
He may turn his ire toward you next, Zenos.

19:17.710 --> 19:20.450
I'd rather avoid any trouble,

19:20.450 --> 19:22.720
but if this guy really does show up,

19:22.720 --> 19:25.890
I'll hit him with a bill for 
all the trouble he's caused.

19:27.480 --> 19:29.650
It's reassuring to know he's out there.

19:29.650 --> 19:30.380
Yeah.

19:31.160 --> 19:35.350
And if I'm being honest, 
I'm a bit jealous that Mr. Zenos

19:35.350 --> 19:38.110
went out of his way to come and visit you.

19:38.110 --> 19:40.820
Being honest with me, eh?

19:40.820 --> 19:43.470
But it was likely for Umin's sake.

19:43.470 --> 19:45.370
I like that even less.

19:45.370 --> 19:48.820
She was a part of my minor laboratory,

19:48.820 --> 19:50.620
on top of being my niece.

19:50.620 --> 19:55.320
My being under suspicion of murder 
puts her in a precarious position,

19:55.840 --> 19:58.640
which is why he wanted my 
innocence on the record.

19:59.210 --> 20:01.970
He'd go so far for that girl?

20:01.970 --> 20:04.110
"I'd pick up all the coins."

20:04.630 --> 20:06.470
Something Zenos said.

20:06.970 --> 20:08.730
All the coins...

20:09.230 --> 20:14.520
The lives he intended to save didn't just 
include the poisoned healers, but Umin, as well.

20:15.180 --> 20:16.460
Even Goldran.

20:16.460 --> 20:18.840
He could've ignored him and let him die,

20:18.840 --> 20:21.240
so he was saved in a sense, as well.

20:21.240 --> 20:26.620
In that case, I'd say you were 
one of those coins, as well.

20:30.070 --> 20:32.550
He really is a remarkable fellow.

20:36.710 --> 20:39.200
I was looking forward 
to this experiment, too.

20:39.910 --> 20:43.630
Zenos, you and I just keep 
running into each other.

20:44.220 --> 20:49.850
How do people think and react 
in extreme circumstances?

20:49.850 --> 20:54.310
I could've gained even more valuable 
data if he hadn't gotten in the way.

20:56.690 --> 21:00.570
Afread, this vessel of yours isn't bad at all.

21:01.280 --> 21:04.730
You'll be staying with me a bit longer.

21:09.850 --> 21:10.730
Well, I'm off.

21:11.330 --> 21:14.580
You're the one who prevented 
the group poisoning.

21:14.580 --> 21:20.360
I hate that everyone being half-conscious 
means you won't get the credit for it.

21:20.360 --> 21:22.090
Ditto.

21:22.090 --> 21:25.680
Nah. This is all the reward I need.

21:25.680 --> 21:27.680
Let's go, Zenos.

21:27.680 --> 21:29.680
Everyone's waiting.

21:29.680 --> 21:31.810
Time to take off, then.

21:31.810 --> 21:33.590
See you around, Umin!

21:34.330 --> 21:36.560
And you, too, my weird big brother!

21:36.560 --> 21:39.620
Right. Thank you both for so much!

21:39.620 --> 21:44.320
Little sis! I'm psyched you finally 
called me "big brother" in the end!

21:44.320 --> 21:47.320
I love ya!

21:57.940 --> 22:00.640
Goodbye, Royal Hospital.

22:01.290 --> 22:05.170
"And so, having resolved the incident, 
Zenos the underground healer

22:05.170 --> 22:08.680
went on to get caught in another mess."

22:08.680 --> 22:11.580
Seriously, stop making ominous declarations!

23:45.920 --> 23:47.150
Coming!

23:48.740 --> 23:50.120
Hello.

23:50.120 --> 23:51.090
Come right in.

23:51.090 --> 23:53.110
Are you a new patient?
